\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.    Rock of Ages, cleft for me,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Let me hide myself in Thee;
\par  Let the water and the blood,
\par  From Thy riven side which flowed,
\par  Be of sin the double cure,
\par Cleanse me from its guilt and power.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par    2.  Not the labours of my hands
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Can fulfill Thy law's demand;
\par Could my zeal no respite know,
\par Could my tears for ever flow,
\par All for sin could not atone:
\par Thou must save, and Thou alone.
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Nothing in my hand I bring,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Simply to Thy Cross I cling;
\par Naked, come to Thee for dress;
\par Helpless, look to Thee for grace;
\par Foul, I to the fountain fly;
\par Wash me, Saiviour, or I die.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. While I draw this fleeting breath,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 When mine eyelids close in death,
\par When I soar through tracts unknown,
\par See Thee on Thy judgment throne,
\par Rock of Ages, cleft for me,
\par \pard     Let me hide myself in Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

